00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:10,160
I'm coming.

266
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:13,720
OK. Here's a list of chores we need to get done.

267
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:16,060
I'll do the dishes and get all the groceries for tonight.

268
00:12:16,420 --> 00:12:17,640
You can sweep and mop the floors.

269
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:19,940
Oh, and the furniture needs to be dusted.

270
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:21,220
You know what?

271
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:23,300
I have to pick something up in the mall.

272
00:12:23,300 --> 00:12:28,120
So why don't you clean the floors and I'll go to the supermarket and get all the groceries.

273
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:29,200
Sure.

274
00:12:29,300 --> 00:12:29,580
That's fine.

275
00:12:30,060 --> 00:12:31,920
Here's the list of all the things you need to get.

276
00:12:33,260 --> 00:12:34,220
Don't forget anything.

277
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:36,560
And can you pick up a bottle of wine on your way home?

278
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:43,180
Hey, honey, I'm back.

279
00:12:44,170 --> 00:12:44,570
Wow.

280
00:12:45,130 --> 00:12:46,330
The house looks really good.

281
00:12:46,730 --> 00:12:46,970
Great.

282
00:12:47,510 --> 00:12:48,210
Can you set the table?

283
00:12:49,930 --> 00:12:50,530
Just a sec.

284
00:12:50,930 --> 00:12:52,690
I'm just going to vacuum this rug real fast.

285
00:12:53,630 --> 00:12:54,990
Wait, don't turn it on.

286
00:13:09,870 --> 00:13:14,050
Has this ever happened to you? Has your vacuum cleaner exploded in your house?

287
00:13:14,430 --> 00:13:16,630
Well, not a big explosion like this one.

288
00:13:16,710 --> 00:13:17,450
Not so dramatically.

289
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:18,730
Not so dramatically.

290
00:13:19,730 --> 00:13:22,490
But I've had this happen to me before.

291
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:23,160
Yeah.

292
00:13:23,160 --> 00:13:24,460
And dust everywhere.

293
00:13:24,460 --> 00:13:25,560
And it's just it's a mess.

294
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:26,280
You don't want to have.

295
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:31,670
You know, this word vacuum is really a very American word.

296
00:13:31,920 --> 00:13:32,440
Yeah.

297
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:32,880
Vacuum.

298
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:33,760
Vacuum the rug.

299
00:13:33,850 --> 00:13:34,370
Vacuum the carpet.

300
00:13:34,560 --> 00:13:35,190
Yeah. Vacuum cleaner.

301
00:13:35,710 --> 00:13:36,910
In the UK, what do they say?

302
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:37,780
Hoover.

303
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:38,880
Hoover.

304
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:39,520
Hoover.

305
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:40,300
Hoover the rug.

306
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:41,200
Hoover the rug.

307
00:13:41,560 --> 00:13:43,700
Which is interesting because it's actually a brand.

308
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:44,420
Yeah.

309
00:13:44,900 --> 00:13:47,660
So I guess it's kind of like American English.

310
00:13:47,760 --> 00:13:49,140
You say, pass me a Kleenex.

311
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:50,120
Oh, that's true.

312
00:13:50,300 --> 00:13:51,440
That would be like a tissue.

313
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:51,880
Yeah.

314
00:13:52,180 --> 00:13:54,720
So I guess they say Hoover the rug or Hoover the house.

315
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:55,960
Yeah.

316
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:56,110
Wow.

317
00:13:56,870 --> 00:14:02,610
You know, I really love these small differences in meaning that we have between American English and British English.

318
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:04,160
Yeah, it's fun.

319
00:14:04,350 --> 00:14:04,510
Okay.

320
00:14:04,830 --> 00:14:08,750
Well, another interesting thing about this is that the man was doing the housework.

321
00:14:08,870 --> 00:14:09,390
I know.

322
00:14:09,910 --> 00:14:10,890
He's a house husband.

323
00:14:11,170 --> 00:14:11,330
Yeah.

324
00:14:11,730 --> 00:14:14,190
So he's the one doing all the chores in the house.

325
00:14:14,370 --> 00:14:16,630
Yeah, that's well, that's the new trend now.

326
00:14:16,830 --> 00:14:22,160
Now it's more popular for men to stay home and take care of the babies and clean the house.

327
00:14:22,460 --> 00:14:22,600
Yeah.

328
00:14:22,780 --> 00:14:27,460
Like when I was growing up, my dad would take out the garbage and that was it.

329
00:14:28,620 --> 00:14:30,280
My mom had to do everything else.

330
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:38,720
But now I think it's becoming a lot more common in especially in North America for the household chores to be divided between the man and the wife equally.

331
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:40,580
Yeah, I think it's fair.

332
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:40,760
Me too.

333
00:14:41,160 --> 00:14:41,600
Yeah.

334
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:42,520
You'd make a good husband, Marco.

335
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:45,620
That's what they say, but they haven't married me yet.

